# HITL test flow (record/overdub)

Use this exact flow whenever running or validating the local hardware-in-the-loop MIDI automation baseline.
Transition verification is always required for baseline validation in this repository.

## Canonical test command

**Default:** assume `teensy41-capture-serial` is already on the device. HITL does **not** build or upload unless you pass `--build-upload`.

Preferred entry point: `host_midi_hitl.py run --preset base` (legacy `host_midi_automation_baseline.py` delegates to the same preset). See [`docs/Plans/hitl_modular_scenarios_enhancement.md`](docs/Plans/hitl_modular_scenarios_enhancement.md).

### Default — managed dual-session (one command)

`host_midi_hitl` **spawns `capture_session.py` and HITL** as two background processes. You do **not** open a second terminal or pass `--follow-current-session`.

```bash
.venv/bin/python scripts/host_midi_hitl.py run --preset base \
 --midi-out "Teensy" --midi-in "Teensy" \
 --track-number 5 --loop-slot 1 --midi-channel 5 \
 --record-bars 2 --overdub-bars 2 \
 --no-fixed-grid-notes --start-transport \
 --overdub-start-delay-bars 0 --overdub-start-delay-beats 1 \
 --phase-wait-ms 500 --final-wait-ms 3000 --press-ms 120 \
 --undo-redo-delay-ms 3000
```

Capture defaults: `--capture-port /dev/cu.usbmodem154944801` (no boot wait by default; pass `--capture-boot-wait N` if needed). Console prefixes: `[hitl-capture]` / `[capture]` for the capture process, `[hitl]` / scenario logs for MIDI.

Layered first smoke (`record_overdub` only):

```bash
.venv/bin/python scripts/host_midi_hitl.py run --layered --preset base \
  --midi-out "Teensy" --midi-in "Teensy" \
  --track-number 5 --loop-slot 1 --midi-channel 5
```

Layered UIP gate preset:

```bash
.venv/bin/python scripts/host_midi_hitl.py run --layered --preset uip_5_5 \
  --midi-out "Teensy" --midi-in "Teensy" \
  --track-number 5 --loop-slot 1 --midi-channel 5
```

Verify-only replay (no device, no capture spawn):

```bash
.venv/bin/python scripts/host_midi_hitl.py run --preset base \
 --verify-serial-log "$(cat captures/.current_session)" --verify-only \
 --track-number 5 --midi-channel 5 --record-bars 2 --overdub-bars 2
```

### Opt-in — built-in serial (single process)

Pass `--no-managed-capture` and `--serial-port`. Do **not** run `capture_session.py` at the same time.

```bash
.venv/bin/python scripts/host_midi_hitl.py run --preset base \
 --no-managed-capture \
 --midi-out "Teensy" --midi-in "Teensy" \
 --serial-port /dev/cu.usbmodem154944801 \
 --boot-settle-ms 10000 \
 --track-number 5 --midi-channel 5 \
 --record-bars 2 --overdub-bars 2 \
 --no-fixed-grid-notes --start-transport \
 --overdub-start-delay-bars 0 --overdub-start-delay-beats 1 \
 --phase-wait-ms 500 --final-wait-ms 3000 --press-ms 120 \
 --undo-redo-delay-ms 3000
```

Undo/redo after overdub stop is **on by default** (3 s wait, double-press undo, 3 s wait, triple-press redo — long loops need deferred save to finish before button presses). Use `--no-undo-redo-after-overdub-stop` to skip.

A **second overdub pass** is **on by default** (2 bars, C0–B1 / MIDI 12–35, 1-beat step and gate, 1-beat start delay). Use `--second-overdub-bars 0` to run record + single overdub only.

**Other tracks:** keep timing/note args unchanged; swap track and channel only, e.g. `--track 4` (sets `--midi-channel 4` automatically) or `--track 4 --midi-channel 4`. `--track-number` is an alias for `--track`.

Long runs (e.g. 32+32 bars) rely on serial heartbeat abort (default 20s silence)
instead of a hard wall-clock timeout. Use `--max-run-seconds N` only if you want
an optional hard cap.

Undo/redo still runs after the **last** overdub stop (tests most recent pass).

**Never mix capture owners:** do not pass `--serial-port` on a managed run (default). Use `--no-managed-capture` first.

**Built-in serial close:** after `final_wait_ms`, the script drains trailing USB serial for up to `--serial-close-drain-ms` (default 10s) until no new lines for `--serial-close-idle-ms` (default 750ms), then snapshots and closes the port. Closing USB serial still reboots the Teensy (expected); the drain captures deferred undo/redo/`#CAP` lines from the firmware TX ring first. Increase `--serial-close-drain-ms` on long undo/redo or persistence-heavy runs if verification misses tail markers.

## Clock and transport proxy

Firmware **does not** log per-pulse MIDI clock (`0xF8`) in `#CAP,MI,...` lines (hot-path cost). HITL uses two separate mechanisms:

| Check | Source |
|-------|--------|
| `*_clock_pulses_seen` (192 gates) | Host **USB MIDI in** clock poll, **or** wall-clock tempo proxy when serial capture shows transport |
| Serial first-note offset / transitions | `#CAP` lines: `ST,Track`, `MI,U` notes, `BPM`, `BAR` |

When managed capture (default) or `--serial-port` is active and recent `#CAP,BPM` or `#CAP,BAR` lines appear, the host paces bar-synced phases via **wall-clock tempo proxy** (prefers BPM from serial tail, else `--tempo-bpm`). Console shows `[info] Bar sync via wall-clock tempo proxy`.

Shared modules: `scripts/hitl/transport_clock.py`, `scripts/hitl/serial_transport.py`, `scripts/hitl/serial_timing.py`.

## Required pass criteria

The run is considered valid only when all are true:

- `record_notes_sent = 32`
- `overdub_notes_sent = 16`
- `record_clock_pulses_seen = 192`
- `overdub_clock_pulses_seen = 192`
- `second_overdub_clock_pulses_seen = 192` (default second pass enabled)
- `second_overdub_notes_sent >= 7` (2 bars × 4 beats − 1 grid tolerance)
- serial verification reports first-note timing within thresholds:
 - `record_first_note_offset.offset_clocks <= record_first_note_max_clocks` (default `12`)
  - `overdub_first_note_offset.offset_clocks <= overdub_first_note_max_clocks` (default `12`) — uses **capture latency** (raw offset minus `--overdub-start-delay-*` / `--second-overdub-start-delay-*` grid delay)
 - `second_overdub_first_note_offset` capture latency clocks `<= overdub_first_note_max_clocks` (default `12`; same grid-delay subtraction as overdub)
- transitions include:
 - `ARMED -> RECORDING` (or `EMPTY -> RECORDING` / `STOPPED -> RECORDING` after clear + transport restart)
 - `RECORDING -> STOPPED_RECORDING`
 - `STOPPED_RECORDING -> PLAYING`
 - `PLAYING -> OVERDUBBING` (≥ 2)
 - `OVERDUBBING -> PLAYING` (≥ 2)
- serial `VERIFY second overdub on/off/open/out/seq` — matched pairs, notes in range
- `VERIFY stored second overdub span (SEVT ticks)` — `count_ok` and `span_ok`
- undo/redo after overdub stop (default on): serial logs include `Overdub undone` and `Overdub redone` (≥ 1 each)

## Serial verification policy (mandatory)

Serial capture must run at the same time as the test for every validated baseline run.

**Default:** managed dual-session — `host_midi_hitl` spawns `capture_session.py` automatically.

**Opt-in built-in serial:** `--no-managed-capture` + `--serial-port` (no external capture).

Do not treat a run as verified if serial capture failed (`Device not configured`), transition lines are missing, or first-note timing checks fail.

## Upload/build behavior for this flow

- **Default:** HITL does not build or upload. Flash manually when firmware changed: `pio run -e teensy41-capture-serial -t upload`
- **Opt-in:** pass `--build-upload` to `host_midi_hitl.py` (upload resets Teensy; managed capture restarts on the next run)
- Do not upload automatically unless the user confirms or passes `--build-upload`
- If USB/MIDI disappears, check `pio device list` and retry only after ports are visible again
